{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '155,192p' KC-Chomp-Chase-KC-Munchkin-gpt-6.1-sol-ultra-20261106-022440/vendor/engine/API.md; cat KC-Chomp-Chase-KC-Munchkin-gpt-6.1-sol-ultra-20261106-022440/vendor/engine/docs/ASSETS.md | head -65; sed -n '1,140p' KC-Chomp-Chase-KC-Munchkin-gpt-6.1-sol-ultra-20261106-022440/vendor/engine/kits/arcade.js\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '155,192p' KC-Chomp-Chase-KC-Munchkin-gpt-6.1-sol-ultra-20261106-022440/vendor/engine/API.md; cat KC-Chomp-Chase-KC-Munchkin-gpt-6.1-sol-ultra-20261106-022440/vendor/engine/docs/ASSETS.md | head -65; sed -n '1,140p' KC-Chomp-Chase-KC-Munchkin-gpt-6.1-sol-ultra-20261106-022440/vendor/engine/kits/arcade.js\"","aggregated_output":"- `r.w(x, y, z)` = buffer pixel of a world point. `r.W`, `r.H`, `r.ix`, `r.iy` (pass to dither functions), `r.view`, `r.visible(x, y, z)`.\n- X-ray: `r.actor(..., { xray: true })` shows the actor's hidden part, a translucent tint with a 1-px outline (a checker in `E.style.trans = 'dither'`), wherever a wall, a prop or shape at least chest high (22; `hides: true | false` says otherwise) or anything queued with `{ hides: true }` is drawn in front of it; not by one rising less than 8 above its feet (the roof it stands on, a cut-down wall). `xray: { color, outline (false: none), actors: true }`: with `actors` other bodies in front hide it too (a hero stays findable in a crowd). Afterimages: `ghost: { color, life, alpha, owner }`; `owner` (the actor's `{x, y, z}`) keeps a trail left nearer the camera sorted behind the live body.\n- Glowing things you draw yourself: `r.queue(x, y, z, fn, { emissive: true })` is drawn again after lighting so darkness never dims it (flames, lasers, magic, neon). It still hides behind whatever stands in front of it: walls and `r.actor` bodies do this on their own, and any other queued draw can join them with `{ solid: true }`. (Canvas lighting builds a depth-ordered mask for this; `game.r.glowMask = false` skips it on slow machines.)\n\n## Pixels, sprites, text, UI\n- `px.rect(g, x, y, w, h, c)`, `dot`, `line(g, x0, y0, x1, y1, c, width)`, `disc(g, x, y, r, c)`, `ell`, `poly(g, pts, c)`, `polyDither(g, pts, c, 0..1, r.ix, r.iy)`, `ddisc`, `sprite(g, spr, x, y, flip)` (or `{ flip, rot, scale }`), `glow(g, 0..1)` (GPU glow for what follows).\n- Sprites from strings (for coins, bullets, ships, icons, NES-style enemies): `const COIN = E.sprite(['.yy.', 'yYYy', '.yy.'], { y: '#f0b020', Y: '#fff0a0' }, scale)`. `.` and space are transparent. Frames: `const walk = E.anim([f1, f2, f3], 8, { pingpong })` (or one sheet: `E.anim(sheet, 8, { frames: 4 })`), drawn with `r.sprite(x, y, z, walk, { t })`. `r.sprite(..., { rot: angle, scale })` turns and scales in whole pixels (cached in 16 steps a turn; `steps: 32`); `E.recolor(spr, { '#3a8a4a': '#8a3a4a' })` swaps a palette.\n- Font (5x7 proportional with lower case: ASCII, the face buttons, arrows, ★ ♥ ♪ ✓ … ° € £, the accented Latin letters; any other is `?`; `font: 'tiny'` for 3x5): `E.font.text(g, str, x, y, color, { outline, shadow, gradient, scale, align, wrap, font })`, `E.font.title(g, str, x, y, { scale, colors, outline, depth, depthColor, align })`, `E.font.width(str, opts)`, `E.font.lineHeight(opts)`, `E.font.wrap(str, maxW, opts)`. Glyphs: ASCII plus `♥ ★ ← → ↑ ↓ • × ♪ ▸ ©`.\n- UI (inside `r.overlay(g => ...)`): `E.ui.box(g, x, y, w, h, { bg, border, gradient, alpha })` (a gradient window like Final Fantasy; `bg` can be `[top, bottom]`, `gradient: false` for flat, `alpha: .6` for a see-through HUD panel), `E.ui.bar(g, x, y, w, h, 0..1, color)`, `E.ui.hearts(g, x, y, hp, max)` (half hearts allowed), `rig.drawPortrait(g, x, y, size, { zoom: 3, turn: .6, bg, frame, cape: false, weapon: false, tint: '#808080' })` (character close-up; it stays upright while the rig kneels or lies down; `tint` greys out a KO'd hero).\n- Dialog: `const talk = new E.Dialog(game)`; `talk.say(['Line one.', 'Page two.'], { name: 'ELDER', portrait: elderRig, onDone, choices: ['YES', 'NO'], onChoice(i) })` (choices show on the last page: the keys, or a tap or click on one, pick); in update `if (talk.update(dt)) return;` (true while a modal box is open: play waits); in draw `talk.draw(r)`. `portrait` takes a Humanoid (live close-up; `portraitSize: 40`, `portraitOpts: { zoom, turn }`) or a function `(g, x, y, size) => {...}`. Radio chatter during play: `talk.say('Enemy fighters ahead!', { name, portrait, auto: 2.5, modal: false })` turns its pages and closes by itself while the game keeps running. Per line: `place: 'top' | 'middle' | 'bottom'`, `y` (pixels) and `alpha` (see-through box). `new E.Dialog(game, { speed, lines, color, nameColor, voice, width, bg, border, vars })` (`voice`: a sound, or `(ch, i, talk) => {}` per letter); `talk.close()`, `talk.open`. Markup in the text: `{c=#ffd36a}gold{/c}` a color, `{w=.5}` a pause, `{s=12}slowly{/s}` letters a second, `{shake}..{/shake}`, `{wave}..{/wave}`, `{$name}` a value from `say(text, { vars })` or `talk.vars`.\n- Menu: `const menu = new E.Menu(game, ['START', { label: 'LOAD', disabled: true }], { x: 'center', y: 100, title, onPick(i, item), onCancel, scale: 2, rows: 6 })` (rows: it scrolls); `menu.update(dt)`; `menu.draw(r)`. Keys, d-pad and sticks move it; a click or tap on an entry picks it (so a phone can leave a title), and the mouse over one moves the cursor. A tap on a dialog box turns its page as confirm does.\n- HTML screens and HUD: `const ui = new E.Shell(game, { theme: { scale: 2 } (a TV; or `tv: true`), settings, screens: { pause, help, dev: { rows: ['glyphs'] } } })`; `ui.show('title' | 'results' | 'map' | ..., spec)`; each step `ui.hud({ objective, status, bars, prompt, minimap })` (`minimap: { map, fog, camera: true, markers, onClick(x, y) }`); `ui.toast(title, text)`.\n\n## Sound: `game.audio` (chip synth, no files, starts after the first key press)\n- `sfx(name, { vol, pitch, pan, loop })` → `{ stop(), set({ pan, vol }) }` (a loop sounds on: an engine, rain). Presets: `jump jump2 land step coin pickup key powerup oneup heal hit hurt stomp bump swing whoosh punch kick shoot laser charge explode boom door secret warp die select confirm cancel pause text blip`.\n- Custom: `sfx({ wave: 'square' | 'pulse' | 'pulse12' | 'triangle' | 'saw' | 'sine' | 'noise', freq: 440 or 'A4', to: 880, dur: .2, vol: .3, arp: [0, 4, 7], step: .05, vib: [8, .03] })`, or `audio.define('zap', voice)`; `audio.instrument('pluck', (ctx, bus, time, freq, dur, vol) => ...)` is a `wave` too.\n- Music: `music('title' | 'adventure' | 'dungeon' | 'boss' | 'victory')` (built in; any other name warns and plays nothing), or your own `{ bpm: 120, steps: 4, tracks: [{ wave: 'square', vol: .15, notes: 'C5 - E5 - G5 . . . | ...' }, { wave: 'triangle', notes: '...' }, { wave: 'drums', notes: 'k . h . s . h .' }] }`. Tokens: a note (`C4`, `F#3`, `Bb2`), `-` holds, `.` rests, `|` is ignored; drums `k s h o c t`. `music(null)` stops. `mute()`, `setVolume(0..1)` (or set `audio.musicVolume`, `sfxVolume`, then `audio.applyVolume()`), `duck(on)` (quieter music under your own pause or map screen). Your own Web Audio connects to `audio.bus('sfx' | 'music' | 'voice')`, under the volume and mute.\n- The music clock (the full engine): a song's place is game time, headless too, and the sound follows it. `music(song, { sync: true })` pauses with the game (else it plays on); `audio.pos` → `{ t, step, beat, bar, at, loop, bpm, layers, playing }`; `at(step, fn)`, `onBeat(fn)` (on the update step); `tempo(bpm)`; `layer(name or index, vol, fade)` (a track's `name`, `on: false` starts it silent: the chase's drums in by layers); `music(song, { fade: 1 })` crossfades; `sting(song, { at: 'bar' })` over the music; `sfx(voice, { step })` on a step of the music. `settings.audioOffset` (ms, Settings, Sound: Calibrate) sets `audio.offset`; `audio.calibrate()` → `{ tap(), result, done, stop() }`.\n\n## Levels\n**TileMap** (top-down, isometric, brawler): walls stand on the ground plane.\n- `new E.TileMap({ rows, legend, types, floorTex, block: ['water', 'lava'], ao: 5, outside })` (`ao` = width of the contact shadow along wall bases, 0 = none; `outside`: the ground past the map, a color, or `false` for none). `types[id] = { h, top, side, line, course, cut: true, cutH, face, roof, beam }` (`cut` lowers walls that block the camera, those `map.isFront(cx, cy, view)` says; a map may replace it; `face`: `'brick'` (default) `'stone' 'rock' 'plank' 'timber' 'plaster' 'hedge' 'none'`; `roof`: `'speckle'` (default) `'plain' 'tiles' 'slab' 'leaves' 'grass'`; `beam` = timber color). `floorTex(x, y, floorTag, view)` returns `[r, g, b]` (or `[r, g, b, glow]`); ready-made: `E.tex.flagstone`, `grass`, `dirt`, `water`, `planks`, `checker`, `plain`. A map of more than 128 x 128 cells bakes its floor in squares as the camera comes to them and lets the far ones go (`chunks: true | false` to choose; `map.floorBytes()` what it holds), so a 256 x 256 world map costs what the screen shows.\n- Legend values: a number = wall type, a string = spawn tag, `{ tile, floor, spawn, block }` for both. `block: true` (or the map's `block` list of floor tags) makes deep water, lava or pits stop walkers (jumping bodies pass over); `walkable(cx, cy)`, `block(cx, cy, on)` (a bridge appears). FlowField paths go around blocked cells and follow `block` and `set` at their next `update`.\n- `find(tag)` / `findAll(tag)` give `{ x, y, z, cx, cy }`. Also `cell(cx, cy)`, `set(cx, cy, id)` (open doors), `toCell(x, y)`, `center(cx, cy)`, `heightAt(x, y)`, `floorAt(x, y)`, `groundAt(x, y, r, z)`, `collide(body)`, `los(x0, y0, x1, y1)` (ground only), `bounds(view)` (`{ x0, y0, x1, y1 }`, buffer pixels), `drawFloor(r)`, `queueWalls(r)`.\n\n**Heights** (collision, standing, sight, reach and navigation share one rule): a body's `z` is its feet; a cell's top is `map.height(cx, cy)` (0 = floor); a body stands on the highest top within `z + 2`. Eyes at `z + E.HEIGHTS.eye` (30) see a target at `z + E.HEIGHTS.chest` (22); a body's own `eye` / `chest` override them (crouching). Same level: `|dz| <= 8`. On a TileMap (`dir` = an angle or `[dx, dy]`): `ray(a, b, { eye, target })` → `{ clear, t, x, y, z }`, `sight(a, b)`, `standable(x, y, z, r)`, `ledge(from, dir)` → `{ x, y, z, rise, facing, edge }` (climb), `landing(from, dir)` → `{ x, y, z, d }` (a jump across a gap), `drop(from, dir)` → `{ x, y, z, fall }`, `arcClear(a, b, apex, r)`, `pick(sx, sy)` → `{ cx, cy, z, face }` (the cell under a screen point: `input.clicked()`, any view and turn). Helpers: `E.sameLevel(a, b)`, `E.targets(from, list, { range, arc, dz, sight: map })` → `[{ target, d, dz, angle }]` nearest first, `E.inArc(..., dz)`. `new E.FlowField(map, { climb, drop, jump })` paths over roofs, between levels and across gaps.\n\n**PlatformMap** (side-scrollers; 2.5D in tilted views): tiles on the x/z plane, top row first.\n- `new E.PlatformMap({ rows, legend, types })`. `types[id] = { kind, style, side, top, line, mat }` (`mat`: any material for a solid tile's face). Example: `rows: ['      ?    ', '   ===     ', '@  g   ^^  ', '###########']`, `legend: { '#': 1, '=': 2, '?': 3, '^': 4, '@': 'hero', 'g': 'walker' }`, `types: { 1: { style: 'ground', side: '#8a5a32' }, 2: { kind: 'oneway' }, 3: { style: 'bonus', side: '#e8a830' }, 4: { kind: 'hazard' } }`. Kinds: `'solid'` (default), `'oneway'` (jump up through), `'ladder'`, `'slope'` (`dir: 1` rises to the right, `-1` to the left; `from` / `to` heights 0..1 for gentle slopes), `'hazard'` (spikes, lava), `'deco'`, `'back'` (background wall). Styles: `'stone'` (`moss`) `'brick' 'wood' 'metal' 'ground'` (`flower`) `'block' 'pipe' 'bonus' 'plank' 'spikes' 'ladder' 'liquid' 'plain'`.\n- Spawns: `find(tag)` gives `{ x, z }` with z = the bottom of that cell (feet). Standing on the ground means z = the top of the floor tiles (`level.groundBelow(x, z)`, which returns `null` over a pit), not z = 0. `cell(cx, cz)` / `set(cx, cz, id)` count cz from the bottom row. `slopeZ(cx, cz, x)`, `touching(body, 'hazard')`, `cellsTouching(body, kind)`, `groundBelow(x, z)`, `solidAt(x, z)`, `move(body, dt, solids)`, `bounds(view)`, `draw(r)` (call first, after `r.sky`), `width`, `height`.\n\n## Movement and physics\n**Platformer** (side-scroller character): `const hero = new E.Platformer({ x, z, w: 8, h: 22, run: 95, jump: 285, gravity: 800, airJumps: 0, wallJump: false, dash: 0 })`.\n- Each update: `hero.update(dt, level, game.input, movingPlatforms)`. For enemies pass `{ x: -1..1, jump, jumpPressed, up, down, dash }` instead of the input.\n- Read: `onGround`, `jumped`, `landed`, `facing` (1 or -1), `air`, `climbing`, `hitWall`, `hitCeiling`, `bumped` (`{ cx, cz, id }` of a block hit from below). Methods: `knock(dir)`, `rigState(extra)` (feed it to `rig.update`).\n- Built in: coyote time, jump buffering, variable jump height (let go early for a short hop), slopes and small steps (sticks to the ground going down), ladders (up / down), drop through one-way tiles (down + jump), optional double jump, wall jump and dash.\n- Further moves, each on request: `crouch` (down: half as tall, it crawls), `ledge` (catches a ledge falling past it; up climbs), `wallCling`, `momentum` (slopes, a roll, a charged dash); tile kinds `'water'` (it swims), `'rope'` (up grabs it), `'bars'` (it hangs and travels), grip `friction` (ice .15), `carry` (a conveyor), `bounce` (a spring), `crumble` and `respawn` (`level.update(dt)` each step); `hero.swingFrom(x, z)` (a grapple: a pendulum, jump lets go); draw `level.drawWater(r)` after the actors. State: `crouching`, `hanging`, `clinging`, `swimming`, `onRope`, `onBars`, `swinging`, `rolling`; `rigState()` poses them.\n- Moving platforms: `{ x, z, w, h, vx, vz }` boxes you move yourself and pass as `solids`; riders are carried.\n# Objects and materials as data\n\nThe full engine draws still objects (barrels, tables, trees, wells) from a few lines of data, in every view and facing,\nwith the house shading and outline, and gives every surface (floors, wall faces, wall tops, platform tiles, the objects'\nown faces) a material from one open registry. An object costs one to a few hundred tokens of data (the core's median is\n125); you check it headless with one command. Read this card whole before you write one. (The agent edition keeps the\nregistries and ignores the calls: `E.addAssets` returns empty lists, the others null.)\n\n## Use one\n\n```js\n// in draw(r): feet on the point, depth sorted like an actor; its front toward facing\nr.shape('barrel', x, y, 0, { facing: Math.PI / 2 });\n// once, before the updates: bodies stop at it, a body coming down lands on it, one wholly below passes under\nmap.solid('table', 120, 80, 0, { facing: 0 });\n// a sprite of it, for an inventory or a HUD (r.sprite, px.sprite)\nconst icon = E.shapeSprite('chest', { view: 'iso' });\n```\n\n- **r.shape options:** facing (radians, where the front points: 0 east, π/2 south, as written), scale, mats ({ slot:\n  material }), flip (mirrors it x to -x, collision too), params (a generator's: { h: 30 }), bias, hides (default true),\n  light (adds its lights to game.lights), shadow (default true).\n- **map.solid** takes the same id and placement, so one object can feed both calls. Bodies span z to z + h (E.Body's h, 32).\n- **In 3D** the 3D engine draws the same entries, materials and boxes: `world.shape(id, x, y, z, o)` (its header).\n- **Steep views** (top-down) draw shapes from the characters' lower angle, as rigs are drawn. The light comes from the\n  viewer's upper left in every view.\n- **Glow and fire:** a material with glow: 1 ignores the light and stays bright in the dark; an entry's flames ([[x, y, z,\n  w, h]]) draw the engine's animated flame (r.shape only: a sprite has none). Anything else that moves stays a prop\n  (r.prop) or your own code.\n- **Dressing a generated level:** a scene is a few entries as [id, across, forward] from an anchor (a wall spot, forward\n  into the room); place it whole or not at all, each part on free floor, after the level's own random picks and from a\n  seeded stream of its own, so the level stays as its seed builds it (Emberdeep's `src/emberdeep/53-scenes.js`).\n\n## The core library\n\n**Shapes** (sized for a 26-unit hero; generators take params): barrel, crate, chest, table, chair, stool, bench, bed,\nbookcase, shelf, pot, jar, sack, cart, well, sign, lamppost, anvil; fence { len: 16 }, pine { h: 41, tiers: 4 },\ntree { h: 40, seed: 1 }, bush { r: 7 }, grass { h: 6, n: 6 }, rock { r: 7.5, seed: 2 }, crystal { h: 18, seed: 1 }.\n`r.shape('pine', x, y, 0, { params: { h: 30 } })`; `E.SHAPES.barrel.about` says what each is.\n\n**Materials:** woods oak walnut birch crate plank planks wood; stones stone cobble marble granite sandstone slate rock\nbrick flagstone ruin; metals iron steel gold copper bronze metal rusted; clay glazed porcelain; cloth linen burlap wool velvet leather;\nplants bark needles leaves shrub moss straw hedge grass; ground dirt sand snow mud; water ice crystal flame bone shingle;\nwalls timber plaster; tops speckle plain tiles slab; tiles block bonus ground pipe checker.\n\n## Materials on surfaces\n\n```js\nE.MATERIALS.mossy = { color: '#6a7a5a', pattern: 'stones', size: 6 };   // or the shorthand '#6a7a5a stones size=6'\nconst types = { 1: { h: 32, top: '#6a6280', side: '#4a4360', face: 'cobble', roof: 'slate' } };   // TileMap walls\nconst map = new E.TileMap({ rows, legend, types, floorMat: 'flagstone', floorMats: { water: 'water' } });   // floors\nconst level = new E.PlatformMap({ rows, legend, types: { 1: { kind: 'solid', style: 'block', mat: 'mossy' } } });\n```\n\nfloorMats is keyed by the floor tags of the legend ('~': { floor: 'water' }); either stands in for floorTex.\n\nA material is `{ color, pattern, ...the pattern's numbers, ramp, glow, over }`. Its five tones come from `E.tones(color)`\n(or its own `ramp` of five, dark to light); the light picks a band, the pattern moves it a step, so a material works on\nevery surface and in every palette and recolors with one hex. An unknown name warns with the list of names.\nOverlays, the last on top, each in its own color's tones: `over: [['moss', '#5f7a3a', { up: .6 }], ['cracks']]`; moss on\nwhat looks up, cracks (the material a step darker), dirt near the ground (h 6), rust; each takes amount and size.\n\n| Pattern | Numbers | What |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| none | | the light alone |\n// The ARCADE kit's game (a cabinet of three: maze, formation, rocks), readable: the starter's shell (src/starter/00-shell.js), then\n// the slice from line 159 (src/starter/32-arcade.js: its header says what it plays and how), then the start (90-start.js), as the\n// single-file kit holds them between GAME START and GAME END. arcade.html plays it; node kits/test.mjs arcade runs it headless.\n/* ============================== GAME START ==============================\n * MY-3D2DGE STARTER: a title menu and vertical slices, one per genre (a genre kit file holds one; the file with every\n * slice adds an animation lab). Each slice is a complete small game, written to be copied and changed: its own header\n * (below this shell) says what it plays, its keys and touch controls, its deep links and how it works.\n * FULL SCREEN, ANY SHAPE: res: 'ps1', expand: true. 320 x 240 is the least the screen shows; a wider or taller window\n * shows more world (r.W x r.H grows), so every HUD anchors to r.W and r.H, never to 320 and 240, and every level fills\n * what a wide screen or an upright phone shows. Prompts name the player's own keys: prompt('attack', 'Sword').\n * To make your own game: change the slice closest to your genre into yours, with its own title, play and game-over\n * scenes, and delete this menu and the slices you do not use; this shell (the game, its scenes, prompt, best and the\n * proof) stays unless you replace it. Deep links: #<slice> starts a slice, #<slice>/<part> jumps into a part.\n * ======================================================================== */\n(() => {\n'use strict';\nconst E = My3D2dge, { px, clamp, lerp, approach, TAU } = E;\n\n/* ---- SHELL: one game, several scenes. Each slice switches view, keys and resolution on entry ----\n * expand: the picture fills the window, any shape, with no bars: at least 320 x 240 (a slice's res), more on the long side */\nconst game = new E.Game({ canvas: 'screen', res: 'ps1', expand: true, view: 'side', bg: '#07060d' });\nconst P = game.particles, L = game.lights, A = game.audio;\nconst scenes = {};\nlet gpu = null;                               // WebGPU lighting, used by the adventure slice only\nconst best = (k, v) => { const old = E.store.get('best:' + k, 0); if (v > old) E.store.set('best:' + k, v); return Math.max(old, v); };\n// a prompt in the player's own controls, after rebinding: 'J Sword' on a keyboard, 'X Sword' on a pad, 'ATTACK Sword' (the\n// button's name) on a touch screen, where the buttons sit over the bottom corner: touch() says so, to move a prompt off it\nconst prompt = (a, word) => game.input.label(a) + ' ' + word, touch = () => game.input.lastDevice === 'touch';\n// each slice: its scene's id, its title entry, a line about it, and its family (the title groups them under it)\nconst SLICES = [\n  { id: 'adventure', label: 'ADVENTURE', about: 'TOP-DOWN ACTION ADVENTURE', family: 'ACTION ADVENTURE' },\n  { id: 'pointclick', label: 'POINT-AND-CLICK', about: 'RELIGHT THE LIGHTHOUSE ON GULL ROCK', family: 'ADVENTURE' },\n  { id: 'platformer', label: 'PLATFORMER', about: 'SIDE-SCROLLING PLATFORMER', family: 'PLATFORM' },\n  { id: 'metroidvania', label: 'METROIDVANIA', about: 'A WORLD OF ROOMS, ITS MAP, ITS GATES', family: 'PLATFORM' },\n  { id: 'brawler', label: 'BRAWLER', about: 'SIDE-SCROLLING BEAT-EM-UP', family: 'FIGHTING' },\n  { id: 'fighting', label: 'FIGHTING', about: 'ONE ON ONE, BEST OF THREE', family: 'FIGHTING' },\n  { id: 'shooter', label: 'SHOOTER', about: 'VERTICAL SHOOT-EM-UP', family: 'ARCADE' },\n  { id: 'arcade', label: 'ARCADE', about: 'A CABINET OF THREE CLASSICS', family: 'ARCADE' },\n  { id: 'pinball', label: 'PINBALL', about: 'ONE TABLE: RAMP, MULTIBALL, JACKPOT', family: 'ARCADE' },\n  { id: 'kart', label: 'KART', about: 'MODE 7 KARTS, THREE LAPS', family: 'RACING' },\n  { id: 'road', label: 'ROAD', about: 'A COAST ROAD AGAINST THE CLOCK', family: 'RACING' },\n  { id: 'puzzle', label: 'PUZZLE', about: 'FALLING BLOCKS AND FALLING PAIRS', family: 'PUZZLE' },\n  { id: 'rhythm', label: 'RHYTHM', about: 'STEP UP! FOUR LANES, TWO SONGS', family: 'MUSIC' },\n  { id: 'rpg', label: 'RPG', about: 'A JOURNEY: TOWN, WORLD, CAVE, BATTLES', family: 'RPG' },\n  { id: 'roguelike', label: 'ROGUELIKE', about: 'A CRYPT OF TEN GENERATED FLOORS', family: 'RPG' },\n  { id: 'tactics', label: 'TACTICS', about: 'TAKE THE HILL FORT, TURN BY TURN', family: 'STRATEGY' },\n  { id: 'rts', label: 'RTS', about: 'GATHER GOLD, RAISE AN ARMY, BURN THEIR CAMP', family: 'STRATEGY' },\n  { id: 'artillery', label: 'ARTILLERY', about: 'TWO TEAMS OF THREE ON AN ISLAND THAT BLOWS APART', family: 'STRATEGY' },\n  { id: 'sim', label: 'SIM', about: 'BUILD A THEME PARK, KEEP THEM SMILING', family: 'SIMULATION' },\n  { id: 'stealth', label: 'STEALTH', about: 'ROOFTOP STEALTH AND PARKOUR', family: 'ACTION ADVENTURE' },\n  { id: 'sports', label: 'SPORTS', about: 'TWO AGAINST TWO IN THE CAGE', family: 'SPORTS' },\n  { id: 'animlab', label: 'ANIMATION LAB', about: 'EVERY MOVE, SKIN AND VIEW', family: 'TOOLS' }\n];\n/* the camera: each slice's scene says how the player may zoom it, camera: { zoom: [min, max] | false, start, tall }: the\n   engine zooms it with the mouse wheel, - and =, a pinch on a phone and Settings, Camera zoom (the player's own, kept, on\n   top of the slice's start: tall on a phone held upright). Keys every slice shares besides: V changes the camera view,\n   [ and ] turn it (camera.rotate), 0 resets it (the player's zoom too), G toggles GPU lighting, M mutes */\nconst camOpt = () => (game.scene && game.scene.camera) || {};\naddEventListener('keydown', e => {\n  if (e.repeat) return;\n  if (e.code === 'KeyV') { game.nextView(); game.note(game.view.label.toUpperCase() + ' VIEW'); }\n  else if (e.code === 'Digit0') { game.settings.set('zoom', 1); game.resetCamera(); game.note('CAMERA RESET'); }   // (resetCamera draws it at once)\n  else if ((e.code === 'BracketLeft' || e.code === 'BracketRight') && camOpt().rotate) { game.rotateView(e.code === 'BracketLeft' ? -45 : 45); game.note('TURN ' + game.yaw); }\n  else if (e.code === 'KeyM') A.mute();\n  else if (e.code === 'KeyG' && gpu) gpu.enabled = !gpu.enabled;\n});\n\n/* ---- TITLE: a lineup of HD heroes on a torch-lit castle ledge under a dusk sky. The ledge is wide enough for a wide\n * screen and sits on the screen's bottom edge whatever its height; the logo and menu hang from the top ---- */\nconst MID = 480, stage = new E.PlatformMap({ rows: ['S'.repeat(60), 'S'.repeat(60)], legend: { S: 1 },\n  types: { 1: { style: 'stone', side: '#6a5a78', moss: '#4a6a3a' } }, edges: 'open' });\nconst titleBg = new E.Backdrop('castle-night');\nconst HEROES = [   // six heroes, each dressed with the HD rig options\n  { face: 0, rig: new E.Humanoid({ size: 1.25, build: 'heroic', armor: true, hair: 'short', cape: { len: 6, width: 6, seg: 2.6 }, colors: { cloth: '#3a5ab0', cape: '#b02a3a', capeIn: '#5a1020', hair: '#e0b050', trim: '#e8c860' } }) },\n  { face: 0, rig: new E.Humanoid({ size: 1.25, outfit: 'tunic', hair: 'spiky', hat: { style: 'pointed', color: '#3aa050' }, colors: { cloth: '#3aa050', pants: '#e8dcc0', hair: '#e0b040', trim: '#8a5a2a' } }) },\n  { face: 0, rig: new E.Humanoid({ size: 1.3, build: 'bulky', weapon: null, hat: { style: 'band', color: '#e03a3a' }, colors: { cloth: '#f0f0f0', pants: '#2f5fd0' } }) },\n  { face: Math.PI, rig: new E.Humanoid({ size: 1.25, weapon: 'gun', hat: 'cap', sleeves: 'long', colors: { cloth: '#d83a2a', pants: '#2f5fd0', glove: '#f0f0f0' } }) },\n  { face: Math.PI, rig: new E.Humanoid({ size: 1.25, weapon: 'staff', outfit: 'robe', hair: 'ponytail', sleeves: 'long', colors: { cloth: '#6a3ab0', hair: '#c8402a', trim: '#e8c860' } }) },\n  { face: Math.PI, rig: new E.Humanoid({ size: 1.25, build: 'heroic', hood: true, outfit: 'coat', sleeves: 'long', colors: { cloth: '#e8e4dc', coat: '#d8d2c8', trim: '#b02a2a', belt: '#b02a2a', pants: '#4a4a5a', boot: '#3a2e2a' } }) }   // the stealth slice's hooded assassin\n];\nHEROES.forEach((h, i) => { h.x = MID + (i - 2.5) * 35; });\n// the corner's buttons (menu, full screen, the page's ? API) in game pixels: about 170 x 60 CSS pixels at the top right\nconst corner = () => { const S = game.screen, k = S.dpr / S.S; return [170 * k, 60 * k]; };\n// where a HUD's top-right corner ends: left of the corner's menu button while it stays there (a touch screen), else the edge\nconst cornerX = () => { const ca = touch() && game.cornerArea(); return ca && ca.y0 < 40 ? Math.floor(ca.x0) - 4 : game.W; };\n/* ---- THE PROOF (tools/kits-test.mjs runs each slice's twice and compares): proof(id, n, script, state, fresh) enters the\n * slice afresh on a game clock at 0, with Math.random seeded, runs n fixed steps of 1/120 s with script(i, key) pressing\n * keys (key.hold('right'), key.up('right'), key.tap('attack')), and gives a hash of what state() returns: the numbers that\n * say how the run went. fresh(), when given, runs first (seeded): it puts back what the slice keeps between visits. A\n * slice's run(n) is one (__game.scenes.adventure.run(600)): the same number every time ---- */\nconst proof = (id, n, script, state, fresh) => {\n  const was = Math.random, I = game.input, held = new Set();\n  const key = { hold: a => { held.add(a); I.hold(a); }, up: a => { held.delete(a); I.hold(a, false); }, tap: a => I.tap(a) };\n  Math.random = E.rng(7);\n  try {\n    if (fresh) fresh();\n    game.time = 0; game.timeScale = 1; game.go(id, null, { fade: 0 }); game.advance(1 / 120);\n    for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) { script(i, key); game.advance(1 / 120); }\n    const s = JSON.stringify(state()); let h = 2166136261;\n    for (let i = 0; i < s.length; i++) h = Math.imul(h ^ s.charCodeAt(i), 16777619);\n    return h >>> 0;\n  } finally { for (const a of held) I.hold(a, false); Math.random = was; }\n};\n// a proof's walk: every `every` steps it lets go of the directions and holds the next of `dirs`\nconst walk = (i, key, dirs, every) => { if (i % every) return; for (const d of dirs) key.up(d); key.hold(dirs[(i / every) % dirs.length]); };\n// START picks too (the touch START, a pad's Start), as Enter does: any player's\nconst pickOnStart = m => { const P = game.players; if (P.some(I => I.pressed('start'))) { P.forEach(I => I.consumeAll()); m.onPick(m.i, m.items[m.i]); } };\n/** the title's menu for the slices in this file: grouped by family when there are several (FamilyMenu, in 05-families.js:\n *  the reference editions carry it, a genre kit of one slice doesn't), else a plain E.Menu */\nconst menuOf = (slices, o) => new Set(slices.map(s => s.family)).size > 1 ? new FamilyMenu(slices, o) : new E.Menu(game, slices.map(s => s.label), o);\nlet titleMenu = null;   // (made at the start, once the file's slices are known)\nscenes.title = {\n  view: 'side', views: ['side', 'brawler'], input: 'DEFAULT', res: 'ps1',\n  enter() { A.music('title'); game.resetCamera(); game.follow(null); game.cam.room = null; game.cam.bounds = null; if (gpu) gpu.enabled = false; L.enabled = false; },\n  update(dt) {\n    if (!titleMenu.update(dt)) pickOnStart(titleMenu);\n    game.focus(MID, 0, 32 + (game.H / 2 - 42) / -game.view.bz);   // the ledge's top 42 px above the screen's bottom edge\n    const t = game.time;\n    HEROES.forEach((h, i) => {\n      const u = (t * .45 + i * .37) % 3, swing = u < .5 ? { spec: { a0: 1.4, a1: -1.6, z0: 12, z1: 8, reach: 7.5 }, phase: u < .15 ? 'wind' : 'active', u: u < .15 ? u / .15 : (u - .15) / .35 } : null;\n      h.rig.update(dt, { x: h.x, y: 0, z: 32, facing: h.face, vx: 0, vy: 0, attack: swing, point: i === 3 && u < .6 });\n    });\n  },\n  draw(r) {\n    const [cw, ch] = corner(), top = r.W / 2 + 132 > r.W - cw ? Math.round(ch) : 0;   // the logo drops below the corner's buttons where it would reach them (an upright phone)\n    titleMenu.y = 76 + top;\n    titleBg.draw(r);\n    stage.draw(r);\n    for (const x of [MID - 100, MID + 100]) r.prop('torch', x, 0, 32, { size: 1.3, light: false });\n    for (const x of [MID - 53, MID + 53]) r.prop('banner', x, -8, 64, { size: 1.1, color: '#8a1a2a' });\n    for (const h of HEROES) r.actor(h.x, 0, 32, (g, ox, oy) => h.rig.draw(g, ox, oy, r.view));\n    r.overlay(g => {\n      E.font.title(g, 'my-3D2dge', r.W / 2, 12 + top, { align: 'center', scale: 4, colors: ['#fffbe8', '#ffe08a', '#ffb347', '#e0662a'], depth: 3 });\n      E.font.text(g, 'My \"3D\" 2D Game Engine', r.W / 2, 48 + top, '#e8e0ff', { align: 'center', gradient: ['#ffffff', '#c8b8f0'], shadow: '#140c1c', outline: false });\n      E.font.text(g, SLICES[titleMenu.i].about, r.W / 2, r.H - 14, '#ffe7a8', { align: 'center', shadow: '#000', outline: false });\n    });\n    titleMenu.draw(r);\n    const dev = game.input.lastDevice, how = dev === 'touch' ? 'Tap a game to play it' : dev === 'gamepad' ? 'D-pad + ' + game.input.label('confirm') + '   ' + game.input.label('start') + ' menu'\n      : 'Arrows + Enter or click   V view   - = zoom   M mute';\n    r.text(how, r.W / 2, r.H - 26, '#b8b0d8', { align: 'center', shadow: '#000', outline: false });\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '9338,9530p' KC-Chomp-Chase-KC-Munchkin-gpt-6.1-sol-ultra-20261106-022440/vendor/engine/my-3d2dge.js\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '9338,9530p' KC-Chomp-Chase-KC-Munchkin-gpt-6.1-sol-ultra-20261106-022440/vendor/engine/my-3d2dge.js\"","aggregated_output":" * 21d. SHELL  an HTML interface over the game, built from data: the screens (title, pause, settings, help, results, map)\n *    and the HUD pieces (toast, tutorial card, interaction prompt, objective with its distance, status, bars, counts,\n *    minimap) a modern adaptation would otherwise write by hand in HTML and CSS. It shows game state and holds none:\n *    the game passes values in every step and callbacks for the buttons, and it reaches the game only through those and\n *    input actions (a button's act is tapped, as input.bindButtons presses one).\n *      const ui = new E.Shell(game, { theme: { accent: '#d9b77c' }, settings: { items: ['sound', 'volume', 'motion'] },\n *        screens: { pause: { text: () => objective.title }, help: { keys: [['WASD', 'Move'], ['SPACE', 'Climb']] } } });\n *      ui.show('title', { name: 'VESPER', subtitle: 'The Ninth Bell', actions: [['Enter the district', start]] });\n *      every step: ui.hud({ objective: { title, text, at: ledger, from: hero }, status: 'UNSEEN',\n *        bars: [{ value: hp, max: 5, kind: 'pips' }], prompt: near && { key: 'E', label: 'Take the ledger', progress },\n *        minimap: { map, at: hero, markers: [{ x, y, kind: 'diamond' }] } });\n *      ui.toast('Checkpoint', 'The ledger is yours'); ui.show('results', { title: 'The names are safe', stats, medals })\n *    With a pause screen, it opens while game.paused and Resume unpauses. Keys, d-pad, stick and touch move the focus\n *    (up / down / left / right turn a slider or a choice, confirm presses, cancel goes back, pause or Start closes the\n *    menu); while a screen is open the game's input is held back. It honors reduced motion and the safe-area insets, CSS\n *    variables theme it (ink, paper, accent, muted, danger, line, font, titleFont), and a headless game keeps its screens'\n *    names and draws nothing.\n *    THE STANDARD MENU: every game gets one (new E.Game makes this shell for itself, and a game's own E.Shell takes over\n *    from it): the pause screen (Resume, the game's items, Settings, Controls, Full screen, Help, Save session while the\n *    page is recorded, Quit to title with a confirmation), the settings screen (Display, Sound, Comfort and the game's own settings, from game.settings) and the\n *    controls screen (every action's keys and buttons, rebound by pressing the new one, conflicts said before anything\n *    changes; the controller's dead zone, aim, symbols and vibration; the touch buttons' side, size and opacity; restore\n *    defaults). new E.Game({ menu: { items: [['Restart', fn]], settings: [...], controls: { attack: 'Sword', skill:\n *    false }, quit: 'title' } }) adjusts it; menu: false, or new E.Shell(game, { standard: false }), leaves it out.\n * ============================================================================= */\nconst SHELL_CSS = `.esh{position:fixed;inset:0;pointer-events:none;z-index:20;font:14px/1.45 var(--font);color:var(--ink);--sat:env(safe-area-inset-top,0px);\n--pt:calc(14px + env(safe-area-inset-top,0px));--pr:calc(14px + env(safe-area-inset-right,0px));--pb:calc(14px + env(safe-area-inset-bottom,0px));--pl:calc(14px + env(safe-area-inset-left,0px))}\n.esh *{box-sizing:border-box}.esh [hidden]{display:none!important}.esh p{margin:4px 0 0;white-space:pre-line}\n.esh h1,.esh h2{font-family:var(--title);font-weight:600;margin:2px 0 0;line-height:1.05}.esh h2{font-size:26px}\n.esh-pan{background:var(--paper);border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:6px;padding:10px 13px;box-shadow:0 8px 28px #0009}\n.esh-k{font-size:11px;letter-spacing:.16em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--accent)}.esh-m{color:var(--muted);font-size:12px}\n.esh-obj{position:absolute;left:var(--pl);top:var(--pt);max-width:min(330px,58vw)}.esh-obj b{font:600 17px var(--title);display:block}\n.esh-dist{color:var(--accent);font-size:12px;margin-top:4px;letter-spacing:.06em}\n.esh-vit{text-align:right;min-width:120px}.esh-hb{display:flex;gap:6px;pointer-events:auto}.esh-hb button{padding:6px 10px;font-size:11px;background:var(--paper)}\n.esh-st{font-size:11px;letter-spacing:.16em}.esh-st i{display:inline-block;width:7px;height:7px;border-radius:50%;margin-right:6px;background:var(--c)}\n.esh-pips{margin-top:5px}.esh-pips i{display:inline-block;width:9px;height:9px;margin-left:4px;transform:rotate(45deg);background:var(--c,var(--danger))}.esh-pips i.off{opacity:.22}\n.esh-bar{height:4px;background:#ffffff1c;border-radius:2px;overflow:hidden;margin-top:6px}.esh-bar i{display:block;height:100%;background:var(--c,var(--accent));transition:width .2s}\n.esh-cnt{margin-top:6px;font-size:12px;color:var(--muted)}.esh-cnt b{color:var(--ink);margin-left:5px}\n.esh-toast{position:absolute;left:50%;top:var(--pt);transform:translate(-50%,calc(-100% - 30px));transition:transform .35s;max-width:min(420px,80vw);text-align:center}.esh-toast.on{transform:translate(-50%,0)}\n.esh-tut{position:absolute;left:var(--pl);bottom:var(--pb);max-width:min(330px,62vw);pointer-events:auto;padding-right:30px}\n.esh-x{position:absolute;right:6px;top:4px;background:none!important;border:0!important;color:var(--muted)!important;padding:2px 6px!important;font-size:16px!important}\n.esh-pr{position:absolute;left:50%;bottom:calc(var(--pb) + 44px);transform:translateX(-50%);display:flex;gap:10px;align-items:center;min-width:200px}\n.esh kbd{font:700 12px var(--font);border:1px solid var(--accent);border-bottom-width:2px;border-radius:4px;padding:2px 7px;color:var(--accent)}\n.esh-tip{position:absolute;left:50%;bottom:calc(var(--pb) + 100px);transform:translateX(-50%);text-align:center;border-color:var(--danger)}\n.esh-col{position:absolute;right:var(--pr);top:var(--pt);display:flex;flex-direction:column;align-items:flex-end;gap:8px}.esh-place{text-align:right;font:italic 13px var(--title);color:var(--muted)}\n.esh-mini{position:absolute;right:var(--pr);bottom:var(--pb);width:min(176px,28vw);border-radius:6px;border:1px solid var(--line);pointer-events:auto;cursor:pointer}\n.esh-keys{position:absolute;left:50%;bottom:var(--pb);transform:translateX(-50%);display:flex;gap:14px;font-size:12px;color:var(--muted);white-space:nowrap;background:rgba(8,6,14,.62);padding:5px 12px;border-radius:8px}.esh-keys kbd{margin-right:4px}\n@media (pointer:coarse){.esh-keys{display:none}}@media (max-width:640px){.esh-obj{max-width:calc(100vw - 214px)}.esh-toast{left:var(--pl);right:var(--pr);top:auto;bottom:calc(var(--pb) + 124px);max-width:none;transform:translateY(calc(100% + 160px))}.esh-toast.on{transform:none}\n.esh-pr{bottom:calc(var(--pb) + 196px)}.esh-tip{bottom:calc(var(--pb) + 262px)}}\n.esh-sh{position:absolute;inset:0;display:grid;place-items:center;background:#04060acc;pointer-events:auto;padding:calc(var(--pt) + 46px) var(--pr) var(--pb) var(--pl);animation:esh-in .25s;touch-action:pan-y}.esh-ttl{padding-top:var(--pt)}\n.esh-sh *{touch-action:pan-y}.esh-sh input{touch-action:auto}\n.esh .esh-nav{position:fixed;top:calc(8px + env(safe-area-inset-top,0px));z-index:2;width:44px;height:44px;min-height:44px;display:grid;place-items:center;padding:0;border-radius:10px;background:rgba(8,8,18,.6);border-color:rgba(255,255,255,.3);pointer-events:auto}\n.esh-nav.x{right:calc(8px + env(safe-area-inset-right,0px))}.esh-nav.bk{left:calc(8px + env(safe-area-inset-left,0px))}.esh-sw{transition:transform .2s,opacity .2s}\n.esh-mod{width:min(460px,100%);max-height:100%;overflow:auto;padding:22px 24px}.esh-wide{width:min(760px,100%)}\n.esh-ttl{place-items:center start;background:linear-gradient(90deg,#04060aee,#04060a99 50%,#04060a00 85%)}.esh-ttl>div{max-width:min(520px,92vw);padding-left:4vw}\n.esh-ttl h1{font-size:clamp(44px,10vw,92px);letter-spacing:.07em}.esh-sub{font:italic 20px var(--title);color:var(--accent);margin-top:6px}\n.esh-btns{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:8px;margin-top:18px}.esh-tags{display:flex;gap:10px;margin-top:18px;font-size:11px;letter-spacing:.16em;color:var(--muted)}\n.esh button{font:600 13px var(--font);letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--ink);background:#ffffff0f;border:1px solid #ffffff2c;border-radius:4px;padding:10px 14px;text-align:left;cursor:pointer}\n.esh button.pri{background:var(--accent);border-color:var(--accent);color:#16130e}.esh button:disabled{opacity:.4;cursor:default}\n.esh button:focus-visible,.esh input:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--accent);outline-offset:2px}\n.esh-row{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;gap:14px;padding:7px 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line)}.esh-row button{min-width:64px;text-align:center}\n.esh input[type=range]{accent-color:var(--accent);width:140px}.esh-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:auto 1fr;gap:6px 14px;margin-top:12px;align-items:center}\n.esh-stats{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(96px,1fr));gap:10px;margin:16px 0 8px}.esh-stats b{display:block;font:600 24px var(--title)}\n.esh-stats small{color:var(--muted);font-size:10px;letter-spacing:.14em}.esh-med{display:inline-block;margin:6px 6px 0 0;padding:3px 9px;border-radius:12px;border:1px solid var(--accent);font-size:12px}.esh-med.off{opacity:.35;border-color:var(--muted)}\n.esh-sec{margin-top:14px}.esh-emb{font-size:34px;color:var(--accent);text-align:center}.esh-map{width:100%;margin-top:12px;border-radius:4px;cursor:crosshair;display:block}\n.esh-still,.esh-still *{transition:none!important;animation:none!important}@media (prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){.esh *{transition:none!important;animation:none!important}}\n.esh-cornered .esh-col{top:calc(var(--pt) + 50px)}.esh-sh button{min-height:44px}.esh-row{flex-wrap:wrap}.esh-row>span{flex:1 1 150px}.esh-row small{display:block;color:var(--muted);font-size:11px;line-height:1.3}\n.esh-ctl{display:flex;align-item