{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_54","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat >> docs/issues.md <<'EOF'\n| C-001 | critical | TV screenshot and phone input test | canvas retained default300×150CSS size, cropping board and mis-scaling pointer input | full-viewport fixed canvas CSS; desktop/phone rerun pending |\n| I-001 | medium | actual mouse hover browser test | native Shell buttons did not focus on hover | delegated non-touch pointerover focuses actionable native buttons |\n| I-002 | medium | emulated pad reassignment test | intentional solo→couch device handoff looked like disconnection; solo aftercouch retained pad:null | reset primary input identity during explicit seat assignment; real disconnect handling retained |\nEOF\ncat >> ../PROGRESS.md <<'EOF'\n\n## Browser findings and fixes\n- Initial browser suite9passed/5failed; failures traced to3unique implementation defects plus one test locator ambiguity.\n- C-001critical: canvas CSS default300×150 cropped TVboard and broke phone pointer coords. Fixed full-viewportCSS.\n- I-001: native Shell mousehover didn't focus. Added delegated hoverfocus.\n- I-002: deliberate pad→keyboard reassignment triggered disconnect pause; soloaftercouch retained pad:null. Reset primary device state on explicit seat assignment.\n- Test-only Back locator resolves duplicate nav/button; tester fixes selector.\n- Rebuilt after fixes; browser agent rerunning, retaking screenshots. Do not trust earlier screenshots.\n- Expanded Hub run95/95passes including legal first-board clear underloss, revision/foodmask convergence, stalepreviousstage rejection, timeup results exactlyonce. Network13/13passes.\nEOF\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_54","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat >> docs/issues.md <<'EOF'\n| C-001 | critical | TV screenshot and phone input test | canvas retained default300×150CSS size, cropping board and mis-scaling pointer input | full-viewport fixed canvas CSS; desktop/phone rerun pending |\n| I-001 | medium | actual mouse hover browser test | native Shell buttons did not focus on hover | delegated non-touch pointerover focuses actionable native buttons |\n| I-002 | medium | emulated pad reassignment test | intentional solo→couch device handoff looked like disconnection; solo aftercouch retained pad:null | reset primary input identity during explicit seat assignment; real disconnect handling retained |\nEOF\ncat >> ../PROGRESS.md <<'EOF'\n\n## Browser findings and fixes\n- Initial browser suite9passed/5failed; failures traced to3unique implementation defects plus one test locator ambiguity.\n- C-001critical: canvas CSS default300×150 cropped TVboard and broke phone pointer coords. Fixed full-viewportCSS.\n- I-001: native Shell mousehover didn't focus. Added delegated hoverfocus.\n- I-002: deliberate pad→keyboard reassignment triggered disconnect pause; soloaftercouch retained pad:null. Reset primary device state on explicit seat assignment.\n- Test-only Back locator resolves duplicate nav/button; tester fixes selector.\n- Rebuilt after fixes; browser agent rerunning, retaking screenshots. Do not trust earlier screenshots.\n- Expanded Hub run95/95passes including legal first-board clear underloss, revision/foodmask convergence, stalepreviousstage rejection, timeup results exactlyonce. Network13/13passes.\nEOF\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
