{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_59","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"rg -n 'campaign|whole|normal|step\\\\(|debug.command' tests/browser.py; cat docs/coverage.md; sed -n '1,140p' tools/hub/check.py\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_59","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"rg -n 'campaign|whole|normal|step\\\\(|debug.command' tests/browser.py; cat docs/coverage.md; sed -n '1,140p' tools/hub/check.py\"","aggregated_output":"62:                page.evaluate(\"game.debug.command('title')\")\n67:                    \"([players,stage])=>game.debug.command('start',{players,board:stage===null?null:ChompContent.stages[stage],mode:stage===null?'campaign':'custom'})\",\n106:                        \"button\", name=\"Chomp!  /  Solo campaign\", exact=True\n148:                click(\"Chomp!  /  Solo campaign\")\n530:                    \"button\", name=\"Chomp!  /  Solo campaign\", exact=True\n537:                    \"game.debug.command('start',{mode:'custom',board:ChompContent.stages[3]});game.advance(.03,{draw:true})\"\n624:                        \"button\", name=\"Chomp!  /  Solo campaign\", exact=True\n# Mechanic and content coverage\n\nAll boards use `ChompContent` schema version 1: 19×15 cardinal cells, two hero starts, exactly three predator starts, twelve stable food IDs (eight ordinary/four powered), optional paired row-7 tunnels, permanent pen at (9,7), and shared generator/editor validation. Native world tiles are a presentation concern; content is expressed only in cells.\n\n| Stage | Authorship / route character | Mechanics demonstrated | Automated evidence expected |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Nibble Boulevard | Authored broad horizontal loops and staggered islands; easy first bite at (3,1) | Movement, early turns, interception, power reversal, three enemy tells | Legal-input clear, warning and collection traces |\n| Side-Door Supper | Authored vertical islands and side approaches | Paired tunnels, intercepting via opposite side | Tunnel travel and seam encounter checks; stage clear |\n| The Turning Table | Authored long central quadrant blocks and open cross-shaped arms | Rotating pen, a timed route that can beat the long detour | All-state graph connectivity; occupancy and gate cadence checks |\n| Peek-a-Chew | Authored offset ledges and side loops | Disappearing walls, periodic reveal and intentional chirp | Reveal/cooldown/collision echo checks; legal-input clear |\n| Shuffle Snack Shack | Generated deterministically from seed CHOMP-1981 | New validated routes under the same rules | Seed reproducibility, validation and legal-input clear |\n| The Midnight Munch | Authored tight central quadrants plus long side detours | All previous mechanics, final-target interception, ending | Whole-campaign completion under normal movement/lives |\n| Seeded Supper | Bounded randomized wall-segment authoring, three density choices | Repeatable remix with tunnels/gate/invisibility options | Sampled seed validator, identical initial states, bounded fallback |\n| Maze workshop | Three varied known-good templates cloned from campaign | Edit, validate, save/load, import/export and playtest | Invalid-import retention; full editor roundtrip |\n\nEvery authored stage was validated during data authoring. A preliminary 100-seed sample produced connected valid boards without fallback. The final test entry point must repeat the applicable assertions after content changes and owns the authoritative reported pass count. Content graph tests do not replace legal-input playthroughs or browser checks.\n\n## Shared validator\n\n`validate(board)` returns `{ok,errors,stats}`. Errors contain a concise actionable `message` and highlighted `cells`. It checks row dimensions/characters, bounded closed frame with paired tunnel mouths, permanent pen approaches, valid non-overlapping starts, safe enemy distances, twelve unique short food IDs and four powered food, cardinal direction values, reachability in all four gate states, outer connectivity when the pen is excluded, and at least four interception loops. Corrupt non-object imports and malformed food entries are rejected rather than thrown. `importBoard(text)` returns a parsed clone only after full validation; `exportBoard(board)` preserves the complete data schema.\n\n## Generator\n\n`generate(seed,{density:'open'|'normal'|'twisty',tunnels:true|false,gate:true|false,invisible:true|false})` uses a retained seeded PRNG for layout and initial travel. It attempts at most 150 wall placements, rejecting disconnected candidates, insufficient loops or too few floor cells. Food placement selects distinct useful floor cells outside player/predator/pen starts. If final validation ever fails, it returns a validated authored fallback marked `fallback:true` with a developer diagnostic. No game-state randomness depends on cosmetic rendering.\n\"\"\"Run the unchanged official Hub harness and compare real shared maze state.\n\nInvoke using the installed Playwright 1.63 Python interpreter. No package or\nbrowser installation, fixed port, global process lookup, or neighbouring files.\n\"\"\"\n\nimport argparse\nimport functools\nimport http.server\nimport json\nimport pathlib\nimport threading\nimport time\nimport urllib.parse\nimport urllib.request\n\nfrom playwright.sync_api import Error as PlaywrightError\nfrom playwright.sync_api import sync_playwright\n\n\nclass QuietHandler(http.server.SimpleHTTPRequestHandler):\n    def log_message(self, *_args):\n        pass\n\n\nDIAGNOSTIC = \"\"\"() => {\n  const s = window.game?.debug?.snapshot?.();\n  if (!s || !window.AIHub?.active) return null;\n  return {hub:{host:AIHub.isHost, server:AIHub.server === true, me:AIHub.me,\n    players:AIHub.players.map(p=>p.id)}, network:s.network,\n    state:{tick:s.tick,phase:s.phase,revision:s.revision,foodMask:s.foodMask,\n      score:s.score,lives:s.lives,actors:(s.actors||s.players||[]).map(a=>[a.id,a.x,a.y])}};\n}\"\"\"\n\n\ndef stage_boundary(browser, origin, harness, game_name):\n    \"\"\"A legal-input accelerated boundary, separate from campaign-completion proof.\"\"\"\n    failures = []\n    passed = 0\n    page = browser.new_page(viewport={\"width\": 1440, \"height\": 900})\n    query = urllib.parse.urlencode(\n        {\n            \"game\": f\"/{game_name}\",\n            \"auto\": 1,\n            \"players\": 2,\n            \"seed\": 42317,\n            \"latency\": 150,\n            \"jitter\": 50,\n            \"loss\": 5,\n            \"play\": 60000,\n        }\n    )\n    page.goto(f\"{origin}/{harness}?{query}\")\n    host = None\n    deadline = time.monotonic() + 25\n    while time.monotonic() < deadline:\n        for frame in page.frames[1:]:\n            try:\n                if frame.evaluate(\n                    \"!!(window.ChompApp?.net?.isHost && ChompApp.net.live)\"\n                ):\n                    host = frame\n                    break\n            except PlaywrightError:\n                continue\n        if host:\n            break\n        page.wait_for_timeout(80)\n    if not host:\n        page.close()\n        return {\n            \"passed\": 0,\n            \"failures\": [\"stage boundary: host did not enter a live round\"],\n        }\n    boundary = host.evaluate(\"\"\"() => {\n      const a=ChompApp, sim=a.sim, before=sim.snapshot(), revision=sim.revision;\n      let steps=0;\n      while(sim.revision===revision && sim.phase!=='lost' && sim.phase!=='won' && steps<120*300){\n        const intents=Object.fromEntries(sim.seats.map(seat=>[seat,sim.botIntent(seat)]));\n        sim.step(1/120,intents); steps++;\n      }\n      a.state=sim.snapshot();\n      a.net.transition();\n      window.__boundaryBefore=before;\n      window.__finishCalls=[];\n      const finish=AIHub.finish.bind(AIHub);\n      AIHub.finish=result=>{window.__finishCalls.push(JSON.parse(JSON.stringify(result)));return finish(result);};\n      return {steps,seconds:steps/120,revisionBefore:revision,revision:sim.revision,\n        stageIndex:sim.stageIndex,phase:sim.phase,lives:sim.lives,score:sim.score,\n        foodMask:a.state.foodMask,stages:sim.stats.stages,finalCatches:sim.stats.finalCatches,\n        defaultRules:sim.config.playerSpeed===ChompSim.DEFAULTS.playerSpeed && !sim.config.invulnerable};\n    }\"\"\")\n    if (\n        boundary[\"revision\"] > boundary[\"revisionBefore\"]\n        and boundary[\"stageIndex\"] == 1\n        and boundary[\"defaultRules\"]\n    ):\n        passed += 1\n    else:\n        failures.append(\n            f\"stage boundary: legal normal-rule bots failed to clear first board: {boundary}\"\n        )\n    guests = [frame for frame in page.frames[1:] if frame != host]\n    repaired = False\n    comparisons = 0\n    deadline = time.monotonic() + 5\n    while time.monotonic() < deadline:\n        hd = host.evaluate(DIAGNOSTIC)\n        recent = {\n            item[\"q\"]: item[\"state\"] for item in hd[\"network\"].get(\"recentStates\", [])\n        }\n        states = []\n        for guest in guests:\n            gd = guest.evaluate(DIAGNOSTIC)\n            if not gd or not gd.get(\"network\"):\n                continue\n            accepted = gd[\"network\"].get(\"lastAccepted\")\n            if accepted and accepted[\"q\"] in recent:\n                comparisons += 1\n                states.append(\n                    accepted[\"state\"] == recent[accepted[\"q\"]]\n                    and gd[\"state\"][\"revision\"] == boundary[\"revision\"]\n                )\n        if states and all(states):\n            repaired = True\n            break\n        page.wait_for_timeout(80)\n    if repaired:\n        passed += 1\n    else:\n        failures.append(\n            \"stage boundary: guests did not converge on the actual new board under packet loss\"\n        )\n    host.evaluate(\"\"\"() => {\n      const before=window.__boundaryBefore;\n      AIHub.send({v:1,t:'s',q:9000000,r:before.revision,k:before.tick,e:1,b:1,\n        s:ChompNet.packState(before)},{reliable:true});\n    }\"\"\")\n    page.wait_for_timeout(550)\n    stale_rejected = all(\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
