{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_66","type":"agent_message","text":"The built HTML has now completed both solo and co-op campaigns using legal movement, default speeds, and normal lives, then reached victory and retried cleanly. Workshop save/import/playtest, touch controls, pad reconnects, audio output, and attract-mode checks also pass. The latest visual check caught an offscreen title-menu option; I’ve compacted the menu and am verifying the final screens.\n"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_67","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json,pathlib\np=pathlib.Path('../exit-interview.json');r=json.loads(p.read_text())\nr['testingFeedback']=[\n'24 unique findings: 5 exposed by initially failing automated checks and 19 by focused code or visual review; all corrected. Repeated symptoms are counted once.',\n'1 critical issue: the canvas kept its default CSS dimensions, cropping the board and mis-scaling pointer input. Full-viewport sizing and desktop/phone checks verified the fix.',\n'The legal-input whole-campaign playthroughs in the built HTML: solo and co-op each caught all 72 snacks, made all six final catches, reached victory with normal lives and retried cleanly. TV screenshots also exposed the canvas defect.',\n'Static syntax checks caught no gameplay defects and were less informative than actual input, campaign and visual checks.'\n]\nr['sourceInformation']['testing']='One quiet command covers normal legal-input solo/co-op campaigns, 58 generated-board completions, 300 reproducible seeds, final-file Chromium and WebKit, emulated pads/touch, procedural signal checks and official impaired-network/dedicated-host Hub cases; no FPS gate. Physical devices and human listening: unknown.'\nr['sourceInformation']['online']='Authoritative shared-world 1–2-player AI Hub co-op, including dedicated hosting and packet-loss repair; standalone solo and simultaneous couch co-op. No standalone matchmaking service.'\nr['engineFeedback']=[\n'The native shaded Blob rig, pixel palette helpers and controller-aware TV Shell gave the game a coherent base.',\n'The native GridMover retains buffered turns and lacks mid-edge reversal; a tested authoritative graph mover supplies the required feel. Explicit controller reassignment also needed input-identity reset.',\n'A deterministic moving-snack maze simulation shared by solo, simultaneous co-op, bots, workshop playtests and Hub authority.',\n'Keeping rotating gates, wrapping edges, continuous motion and swept encounters consistent across route planning and shared state.',\n'No vendored engine changes. Game-specific movement/topology and focused Shell/input adapters extend the engine externally.',\n'Add a dynamic graph-edge mover and a simultaneous shared-world arcade starter with session-safe menus.'\n]\nr['promptFeedback']=[\n'The source-defining moving food, concrete player outcomes and explicit verification gates kept the game coherent.',\n'The proposed first-run duration is a hypothesis: expert legal bots finish much faster, while first-human playtime remains unknown.',\n'Integrating six stages, a complete controller-usable workshop, procedural presentation and authoritative multiplayer into one direct-open HTML.',\n'Separate mandatory acceptance from optional depth, and distinguish measured completion times from desired first-human timing.'\n]\np.write_text(json.dumps(r,ensure_ascii=False,indent=2)+'\\\\n')\nlines=[x for x in pathlib.Path('docs/issues.md').read_text().splitlines() if x.startswith('| ') and not x.startswith('| ID')]\nassert len(lines)==24,(len(lines),lines)\nassert len(r['testingFeedback'])==4 and len(r['engineFeedback'])==6 and len(r['promptFeedback'])==4\nassert all(isinstance(v,str) and v for v in r['sourceInformation'].values())\nassert r['sourceInformation']['usage']=='added on import'\nprint('Release JSON validated;24uniqueissues,1critical;feedback4/6/4.')\nPY\ncat > docs/feedback.md <<'EOF'\n# Release feedback\n\nThe source-of-truth answers are the root \"'`exit-interview.json`, embedded at build time into the game'\"'s About/Credits. The four required categories are Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback.\n\nThe issue ledger contains24distinct findings, including1critical(canvas CSS sizing). Five were exposed by initially failing automated checks(S-001,C-001,I-001,I-002,U-001);19came from focused code/visual review. Multiple symptoms of the canvas bug count once. Final passing verification replaces earlier failing snapshots; previous counts are retained in PROGRESS.md for history.\n\nWhole-campaign evidence is from ordinary legal player intents with unchanged default speeds, normal five starting lives, actual moving food, damage rules, clear delays and transitions. No food-mask edits, teleportation, stage skips or attract cheats are completion evidence. Efficient bots completed the final built HTML solo in177.43simulatedseconds and co-op in127.81seconds in the recorded browser trace. First-human12–18minute pacing is unconfirmed. Human listening quality and physical hardware behavior remain unknown; specified browser/controller/touch stand-ins were used.\n\nThe native engine/client are pinned and unmodified. New systems are the graph-based authoritative simulation, original content/creature details, editor, procedural note/event data, compact network authority adapter and targeted Shell/input composition. Rendering uses the full engine, native pixel helpers, palette tones, actor sorting, Blob squash-and-stretch, shadows, fixed-step Game, TV Shell, Settings, rebinding and audio buses.\nEOF\nnode tools/build.mjs\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
